6. System Architecture

The proposed system can be divided into five major layers.

Layer 1 – Sensing Layer

This layer contains sensors installed throughout the mine. It collects environmental information such as gas concentration, temperature, humidity, smoke, vibration, and water level.

Layer 2 – Worker Monitoring Layer

This layer consists of wearable devices or worker identification tags. It provides information about worker presence and location.

Layer 3 – Communication Layer

This layer transfers data from underground sensor nodes to the monitoring system. Mesh networking or other suitable wireless technologies can be used.

Layer 4 – AI and Processing Layer

This layer processes the incoming data and applies AI-based techniques for anomaly detection and risk analysis.

Layer 5 – Monitoring and Rescue Layer

This is the user-facing layer. It displays the mine status, alerts, worker information, and other important information to the control-room operator and rescue team.

